 f(11,2) = 570 + 10 = \\boxed{580}.$$\n\n### PROOF COMPLETE", "thinking": "Let me solve this problem. I need to find all local extrema of f(x,y) = x³ + 3xy² - 18x² - 18xy - 18y² + 57x + 138y + 290, then sum the function values at all local max and min points.\n\nFirst, answer leak check: The problem text doesn't contain any solution or answer. Good.\n\nLet me compute partial derivatives.\n\nf_x = 3x² + 3y² - 36x - 18y + 57\nf_y = 6xy - 18x - 36y + 138\n\nSet to zero:\n(1) 3x² + 3y² - 36x - 18y + 57 = 0 → x² + y² - 12x - 6y + 19 = 0\n(2) 6xy - 18x - 36y + 138 = 0 → xy - 3x - 6y + 23 = 0 → x(y-3) = 6y - 23 → x = (6y-23)/(y-3)\n\nLet me substitute. From (2): x = (6y-23)/(y-3).\n\nLet me compute. Let me denote. Substitute into (1):\nx² + y² - 12x - 6y + 19 = 0\n\nx = (6y-23)/(y-3). Let me compute x² and 12x.\n\nLet me set t = y. x = (6t-23)/(t-3).\n\nx² = (6t-23)²/(t-3)² = (36t² - 276t + 529)/(t-3)²\n12x = 12(6t-23)/(t-3) = (72t-276)/(t-3)\n\nMultiply (1) by (t-3)²:\n(36t² - 276t + 529) + t²(t-3)² - 12·... wait let me be careful.\n\n(1): x² + y² - 12x - 6y + 19 = 0\nMultiply by (t-3)²:\n(6t-23)² + t²(t-3)² - 12(6t-23)(t-3) - 6t(t-3)² + 19(t-3)² = 0\n\nLet me expand each term.\n\nTerm A: (6t-23)² = 36t² - 276t + 529\n\nTerm B: t²(t-3)² = t²(t² - 6t + 9) = t⁴ - 6t³ + 9t²\n\nTerm C: -12(6t-23)(t-3). First (6t-23)(t-3) = 6t² - 18t - 23t + 69 = 6t² - 41t + 69. So -12· = -72t² + 492t - 828.\n\nTerm D: -6t(t-3)² = -6t(t²-6t+9) = -6t³ + 36t² - 54t\n\nTerm E: 19(t-3)² = 19(t²-6t+9) = 19t² - 114t + 171\n\nSum:\nt⁴: 1\nt³: -6 - 6 = -12\nt²: 36 + 9 - 72 + 36 + 19 = 28\nt¹: -276 + 492 - 54 - 114 = 48\nconst: 529 - 828 + 171 = -128\n\nSo t⁴ - 12t³ + 28t² + 48t - 128 = 0.\n\nLet me try to factor. Try t=2: 16 - 96 + 112 + 96 - 128 = 0. Yes! t=2 is a root.\n\nTry t=4: 256 - 768 + 448 + 192 - 128 = 0. 256-768=-512, +448=-64, +192=128, -128=0. Yes t=4 is a root.\n\nSo (t-2)(t-4) divides. Let me divide polynomial by (t-2)(t-4) = t²-6t+8.\n\nDivide t⁴ - 12t³ + 28t² + 48t - 128 by t² - 6t + 8.\n\nt⁴ - 12t³ + 28t² + 48t - 128 ÷ (t² - 6t + 8):\nFirst term: t². t²·(t²-6t+8) = t⁴-6t³+8t². Subtract: (-12+6)t³ + (28-8)t² + 48t -128 = -6t³ + 20t² + 48t - 128.\nNext: -6t. -6t·(t²-6t+8) = -6t³+36t²-48t. Subtract: (20-36)t² + (48+48)t -128 = -16t² + 96t - 128.\nNext: -16. -16(t²-6t+8) = -16t²+96t-128. Subtract: 0.\n\nSo quotient = t² - 6t - 16. Roots: t = (6 ± √(36+64))/2 = (6 ± 10)/2 = 8 or -2.\n\nSo y = 2, 4, 8, -2.\n\nNow find x for each:\nx = (6y-23)/(y-3)\n\ny=2: x = (12-23)/(2-3) = (-11)/(-1) = 11. Point (11,2).\ny=4: x = (24-23)/(4-3) = 1/1 = 1. Point (1,4).\ny=8: x = (48-23)/(8-3) = 25/5 = 5. Point (5,8).\ny=-2: x = (-12-23)/(-2-3) = (-35)/(-5) = 7. Point (7,-2).\n\nSo critical points: (11,2), (1,4), (5,8), (7,-2).\n\nNow classify using second derivative test.\n\nf_xx = 6x - 36\nf_yy = 6x - 36\nf_xy = 6y - 18\n\nHessian H = f_xx·f_yy - (f_xy)² = (6x-36)² - (6y-18)²\n\nAt (11,2): f_xx = 66-36=30, f_yy=30, f_xy=12-18=-6. H = 900 - 36 = 864 > 0, f_xx=30>0 → local minimum.\n\nAt (1,4): f_xx = 6-36=-30, f_yy=-30, f_xy=24-18=6. H = 900 - 36 = 864 > 0, f_xx=-30<0 → local maximum.\n\nAt (5,8): f_xx = 30-36=-6, f_yy=-6, f_xy=48-18=30. H = 36 - 900 = -864 < 0 → saddle point.\n\nAt (7,-2): f_xx = 42-36=6, f_yy=6, f_xy=-12-18=-30. H = 36 - 900 = -864 < 0 → saddle point.\n\nSo local extrema: local min at (11,2), local max at (1,4).\n\nNow compute f at these points.\n\nf(x,y) = x³ + 3xy² - 18x² - 18xy - 18y² + 57x + 138y + 290\n\nAt (1,4):\nx³ = 1\n3xy² = 3·1·16 = 48\n-18x² = -18\n-18xy = -18·1·4 = -72\n-18y² = -18·16 = -288\n57x = 57\n138y = 552\n+290\n\nSum: 1 + 48 - 18 - 72 - 288 + 57 + 552 + 290\n= 1+48 = 49\n49-18 = 31\n31-72 = -41\n-41-288 = -329\n-329+57 = -272\n-272+552 = 280\n280+290 = 570\n\nf(1,4) = 570.\n\nAt (11,2):\nx³ = 1331\n3xy² = 3·11·4 = 132\n-18x² = -18·121 = -2178\n-18xy = -18·11·2 = -396\n-18y² = -18·4 = -72\n57x = 627\n138y = 276\n+290\n\nSum: 1331 + 132 - 2178 - 396 - 72 + 627 + 276 + 290\n1331+132 = 1463\n1463-2178 = -715\n-715-396 = -1111\n-1111-72 = -1183\n-1183+627 = -556\n-556+276 = -280\n-280+290 = 10\n\nf(11,2) = 10.\n\nSum = 570 + 10 = 580.\n\nLet me double-check f(11,2).\n1331 + 132 = 1463\n1463 - 2178 = -715\n-715 - 396 = -1111\n-1111 - 72 = -1183\n-1183 + 627 = -556\n-556 + 276 = -280\n-280 + 290 = 10. ✓\n\nf(1,4):\n1 + 48 = 49\n49 - 18 = 31\n31 - 72 = -41\n-41 - 288 = -329\n-329 + 57 = -272\n-272 + 552 = 280\n280 + 290 = 570. ✓\n\nSum = 580.\n\nThe answer is 580.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786637419}
